## Problem
All 5 networking question init-spaces files construct class instances with `new GridSpace()`, `new PoolSpace()`, and `new Item()`, then dispatch them into state:

- `tcp/-utils/init-spaces.ts:33`: `const gridSpace = new GridSpace({ id, name, rows, cols, metrics, ... })`
- `tcp/-utils/init-spaces.ts:69`: `const entity = new Item({ id, name, icon, data, allowedPlaces, ... })`
- `tcp/-utils/init-spaces.ts:50`: `const inventorySpace = new PoolSpace({ id: 'inventory', ... })`

After Phase 1 changed CREATE_SPACE to expect `SpaceData` (plain object) and CREATE_ENTITY to expect `EntityData` (plain object), these class instantiations produce the wrong type. The dispatch payloads need to contain plain data objects from factory functions instead.

The same pattern repeats identically in all 5 files: tcp, udp, internet, dhcp, webserver-ssl.

## Goal
Replace all `new GridSpace()`, `new PoolSpace()`, and `new Item()` calls with factory functions `createGridSpaceData()`, `createPoolSpaceData()`, and `createItemData()` in all 5 networking question init-spaces files.

